OK, let me reproduce and observe. Actually — hmm, one candidate to check first: `timeout` itself (pid 2568) was also still alive. If nbd-client had died on TERM, timeout would have exited with 124. Both alive → the client is ignoring/blocking TERM.

Ohhh, wait. I think I've got it! In main() — the ioctl path sets... no. Hmm, what about SIGCHLD? No.

